# Quiet Mode / Event Mode

Product law: `docs/design/Game_Design_Bible_v1.1.1.md`. On conflict, the Bible wins. Law 6.

Exactly **two** presentation states. Every UI feature **must declare** Quiet Mode or Event Mode before it is built (§4.8, §19.1, §24 filter 8). Undeclared surfaces are rejected.

## Quiet Mode (normal WoW)

Render **at most** a hideable minimap. The Nights board is player-opened. The one licensed unbidden cue is a faint glow when the board changed since the player last opened `/beef` or the Nights parchment. Contractual, not aspirational.

**Banned ambient surfaces:** feeds, dashboards, toasts, pips, sound, “now playing,” activity panels, bars, standing tabs, points-history, grant/suggestion toasts during normal play, minimap pips on grants (Audit V9). **“Just a small always-visible panel” is rejected** (§4.8, §19.1).

Quiet Mode is **silent, absolutely** — no ambient audio, UI clicks-and-whooshes, or notification sounds (§19.4).

**Unbidden Quiet chrome** is only the hideable minimap (plus the licensed unseen-change glow). **Player-opened Quiet** is identity/history (profile / records) per §14.2 and the Nights board per §14.1 — not a Standing tab, points history, Ladder, Officer desk, grant pip, petition pip, or always-on chip. Minimap left-click opens the player card; right-click opens the Nights parchment. That is not a license for always-visible chrome or a feed. Do not add extra Quiet Mode surfaces “for usability.” Do not invent Director Console UX here (§18).

A Tuesday login sees **almost nothing.** The week of posted nights is on `/beef`. Do not “fix” the quiet with a feed (§14.2).

## The Nights board (the one Quiet Mode feature beyond presence)

Church nights (Gathering, Knighting night, Gora night) are Pope-posted weekly series; skip/move a week is allowed. Discord raid/PvP stubs are notices with “Sign up on Discord” — no in-addon Going. Congregation Going on Church nights is a public count; names stay on the Pope desk. No login banner. Glow only when the board revision is newer than last view (§14.1).

**Hard bound:** no Discord API, role signup, reminders, toasts, auto-start, or attendance ledger. Do not invent Council designation UX beyond `Data/Council.lua` + `ui.councilOverrides`.

## Event Mode (ceremonies and Goras)

Theatrical: proclamations, cards, HUD, favor, outcomes, sound (§4.8, §19.2). Entered and exited **only** via the ceremony runtime (§20). When the machine returns to QUIET, Event chrome (HUD, cards, favor, ceremonial sound) **must go**. Congregation receives theater, not administration (§18.5).

Rhythm: **Quiet → Ritual Begins → Spectacle → Consequence → Quiet.**

## Sound

Event Mode only. MVP cue names from §19.4 **only**: Sanction bell, Verdict, Elevation, Knighting, Cowardice Recorded; later, Canonization seal. Do not add ambient UI clicks or any other cues.

## Notices and onboarding

Toast-engine, if any: **Event Mode only** (consequence beats). The **only** Quiet exception is the Bible’s gentle version-mismatch notice when a stale client drops to Quiet Mode (§13.4 / §20.3). That is a notice, not a toast-kind family. No other Quiet toasts exist. Do not invent toast kinds.

Onboarding: **one parchment welcome** (Quiet, first launch only), then silence until the Church does something. No config walls, tutorial popups, or minimap fanfare (§19.5).

## Scope filters (§24)

8. Is it Quiet Mode or Event Mode — and does Quiet Mode stay quiet?
9. Does it replace something a human currently performs that is part of the entertainment?

Unfavorable → defer or reject. Do not invent product answers; append `docs/design/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md`.
